From 4fa3294238ac68c1ccab58e7a94d6d83dac98ca7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 02:54:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] freedreno/a5xx: program the highest bank bit of the part

RB_MODE_CNTL and TPL1_MODE_CNTL carry the highest bank bit, which the
kernel programs from the per-SoC UBWC configuration on every
hw_init. Mesa rewrites both with msm8996's value on every batch
and 2D blit, so on SoCs with a different hbb value, such as sdm630,
sdm660 and msm8953, the texture pipe and render backend swizzle with a
different bank bit than UCHE, which keeps the kernel's value.

Describe the HIGHESTBANKBIT field of both registers, and derive it from
highest_bank_bit reported by the kernel.

Fixes: 07e1233c6157 ("freedreno: Enable Adreno 508, 509 and 512")
Fixes: dc6f7045665e ("freedreno: Enable A506")
Fixes: afb7b17fddca ("freedreno: Enable A505")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45481>

Base-commit: b69adc2adfbfe3eb985bd66cd06c61ca719ae9ae
Apply in filename order within this project.
Upstream-commit: 4fa3294238ac68c1ccab58e7a94d6d83dac98ca7
Source: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/commit/4fa3294238ac68c1ccab58e7a94d6d83dac98ca7
Backport: omit the newer computerator tool, which is absent from Mesa 26.2.7; retain the runtime changes and decoder reference updates.
Backport: refresh the existing compute-a540 decoder fixture contexts; preserve this branch's SP_MODE_CNTL decoding and all upstream bank-bit reference updates.

